{"id":"fc43ef3f3e8f150fd056d7ed","source":"meduza-rss","source_name":"Meduza","platform":"rss","url":"https://meduza.io/en/feature/2026/11/17/alexey-kiselev-the-last-editor-in-chief-of-nonfiction-publisher-individuum-gives-his-first-interview-since-its-closure-colleagues-arrests-censorship-and-bots-that-screen-books-for-extremism","published_at":"2026-11-17T00:10:33Z","collected_at":"2026-11-17T00:23:00.592756Z","title":"Alexey Kiselev, the last editor-in-chief of nonfiction publisher Individuum, gives his first interview since its closure: colleagues’ arrests, censorship, and bots that screen books for ‘extremism’","text":"On November 12, the Eksmo publishing group said it was launching a new publisher, Tropy. Its immediate plans include publishing books that never made it into print at Individuum. Like its predecessor, Tropy says it will specialize in nonfiction. Individuum, founded in 2015 as an independent publisher and bought by Eksmo in 2023, closed in September — shortly after its employees charged in the “publishers’ case” each received a suspended four-year prison sentence . Its last editor-in-chief was Alexey Kiselev, a theater critic and curator. Kiselev spoke to Meduza about how Individuum worked under wartime censorship, how its relationship with Eksmo changed after the criminal investigation began, and why reading AI-generated edits became part of his job. — You live in Yerevan. Do you visit Russia? — No, I don’t go back anymore. Once the so-called publishers’ case began, it became clear that if you do public-facing work that involves sharing information, any trip to Russia is extremely unsafe. In May 2025, three people connected to Individuum and Popcorn Books were detained in Russia: former Popcorn Books sales director Pavel Ivanov, Individuum executive director Dmitry Protopopov, and ","html":"","media":[],"author":"","language":"und","group":"international-media","perspective":"mixed","trust":"high","tags":[],"raw":{"archive_policy":"public_excerpt_v1","content_sha256":"5732d9b920372f9c8e15488d476a79af43b270911db5a0cfe10b9d71e109f4f0","original_text_chars":32237,"original_html_chars":1273,"text_truncated":true,"media_count":0,"platform":{"entry_id":"https://meduza.io/en/feature/2026/11/17/alexey-kiselev-the-last-editor-in-chief-of-nonfiction-publisher-individuum-gives-his-first-interview-since-its-closure-colleagues-arrests-censorship-and-bots-that-screen-books-for-extremism","entry_link":"https://meduza.io/en/feature/2026/11/17/alexey-kiselev-the-last-editor-in-chief-of-nonfiction-publisher-individuum-gives-his-first-interview-since-its-closure-colleagues-arrests-censorship-and-bots-that-screen-books-for-extremism"}}}
