{"id":"df129d6826a00b1be3a868bf","source":"guardian-rss","source_name":"The Guardian World","platform":"rss","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/nov/16/donald-trump-asia-visit-democrats-republicans-elizabeth-warren-faa-air-disruption-latest-news-updates","published_at":"2026-11-17T00:19:28Z","collected_at":"2026-11-17T00:23:34.453342Z","title":"Trump defends commerce secretary Lutnick for allegedly slow-walking Nvidia chip export restrictions – live","text":"11.10 EST Trump defends under-fire commerce secretary after allegedly slow-walking export restrictions on advanced AI chips Donald Trump also defended his commerce secretary Howard Lutnick today, after he came under fire for allegedly slow-walking export restrictions on Nvidia chips to China. This comes after the company’s CEO, Jensen Huang, was ousted from his role following a revelation that he had a close relationship with Alice Huang (no relation), allegedly a Chinese operative. Lutnick is now set to testify before Congress about delays by the commerce department in adding Singapore-based Megaspeed, which is associated with Alice Huang and has bought billions of dollars of Nvidia chips in recent years, to Washington’s blacklist of companies that the US considers a risk to national security despite reported concerns within the administration. Today, Trump justified any delayed action by Lutnick, adding that he’s done a “very good” job. “If you didn’t delay it, if you did do something, you could have a blow up with China. We’re having a very good relationship with China right now,” Trump said. Lutnick is currently traveling with the president and other senior officials and cabine","html":"","media":[],"author":"Maanvi Singh (now); Cecilia Nowell, Shrai Popat, Lucy Campbell and Tom Ambrose (earlier)","language":"und","group":"international-media","perspective":"mixed","trust":"high","tags":[],"raw":{"archive_policy":"public_excerpt_v1","content_sha256":"8a49ea44f37bc3d00ce79e7d9c90b0a94db9c1ddebf0b93f056cdea56ae37703","original_text_chars":1739,"original_html_chars":2345,"text_truncated":true,"media_count":0,"platform":{"entry_id":"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/nov/16/donald-trump-asia-visit-democrats-republicans-elizabeth-warren-faa-air-disruption-latest-news-updates","entry_link":"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/nov/16/donald-trump-asia-visit-democrats-republicans-elizabeth-warren-faa-air-disruption-latest-news-updates"}}}
